<Site title="Sample review — MooonStoreClinic"><section class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">SELF-CREATED DEMONSTRATION / NOT A CLIENT CASE</p><h1>What a useful finding looks like.</h1><p class="lede">A fictional cup product page illustrates our report format. No live merchant was tested, no orders were placed and no business results are claimed.</p><div class="sample-grid"><article class="sample before"><span>BEFORE / FICTIONAL PAGE</span><h3>Everyday cups</h3><strong>$18</strong><p>Choose: Small / Large</p><div class="mock-button">Buy now</div></article><article class="sample after"><span>PROPOSED COPY / SAME FICTIONAL PRODUCT</span><h3>Everyday cups · 12 oz</h3><strong>$18 per pack of 50</strong><p>Size: 12 oz · Quantity: 50 cups<br/>Lids sold separately.</p><div class="mock-button">Add 1 pack to cart — $18</div></article></div><div class="prose"><h2>Finding 01 · Clarify what the price buys</h2><p><b>Observed in this demonstration:</b> the original panel shows $18 and “Small / Large”, without a pack quantity or capacity. The proposed panel makes these fictional specifications explicit.</p><p><b>Priority:</b> review before cosmetic changes. These details affect understanding of the offer. No measured sales impact is available.</p><p><b>Recommendation:</b> validate actual quantity, size, inclusions and price with the merchant, then place them near the primary action.</p><p><b>Acceptance check:</b> confirm the visible pack quantity and capacity match the selected variant and actual cart line item on desktop and mobile. That interactive check has not been performed in this static demonstration.</p><h2>What a commissioned report adds</h2><p>Your agreed URL, observation date, viewport, reproducible steps, screenshots, tested states and limitations. We report fewer than three priorities if the evidence does not support three.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Discuss your product page ↗</a></div></section></Site>